# vit_v1_endpoint: ViT-Base/16 with s5_per_layer's lever set and driver, unchanged.
#
# port       driver changes forced by the model only:
#              no attention mask      mask tensor, its encryption and sub-graph removed: 14 sub-graphs
#                                     (BERT driver: 15)
#              no pooler              head = final LayerNorm + CLS slice
#              patch embedding        one pixel_values operand instead of two token tensors
#              local checkpoint dir   image carries only BERT, nodes offline
#            levers byte-identical: param_spill_gpu,param_defer_gpu, spill to /results.
# phase B    pair = vit_v1_endpoint vs vit_v0_default. The BERT mask sub-graph difference (524,288 B,
#            one round) cannot occur here.
# inert      SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 drives embed_chunk_gpu (vocabulary one-hot matmul); ViT has no
#            vocabulary; kept so the set stays unchanged (as SHAFT-CPU-ViT). Not covered by
#            check_lever. SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1 is guarded and announces (MatMul.forward).

BASELINE_SCRIPT=$BASE/vit_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_SCRIPT=vit_perlayer_gpu.py
SHAFT_LIMB_LOOP=1
SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16
SHAFT_LEVERS=param_spill_gpu,param_defer_gpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_PARAM_SPILL=1 SNNI_SPILL_DIR=/results SHAFT_MODEL=/vit SHAFT_MAX_LENGTH=197"
